<https://w3id.org/mailo#P_817_005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "C-817/19 paras 222-227 (PNR Directive Art.12(3)(b)): disclosure after the initial period requires prior review by a court or independent administrative authority, which must be objective, impartial, free from external influence, and distinct from the requesting authority or the PIU. The Court said nothing about GDPR Art.35 or DPIAs; the link from independent prior review to a DPIA obligation for medical AI is an authorial cross-instrument interpretation by the ontology designer, not a holding. The DPIA requirement stands on GDPR Art.35 alone."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#CourtHolding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The encoded proposition is what the court decided, at the paragraphs cited."@en .
