<https://w3id.org/mailo#DGA_Art3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Opens Chapter II (Arts 3-9) by fixing the categories of protected data held by public sector bodies whose re-use the Regulation conditions, including data subject to statistical or commercial confidentiality and personal data. The substantive re-use conditions, including anonymisation and the secure processing environment, are in Art.5. Applies to AI training use cases at hospitals and research institutes. Corrected in v5.1.0 Round 5: previously recorded as Art.2, the Definitions article."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Right_ExpressViews> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/mailo#DataSubjectRight> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#EHDS_Art92> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Independent advisory body facilitating cooperation between Member States and the Commission, with two representatives per Member State (one for primary and one for secondary use). Its remit is consultative. Renumbered in v5.1.0: previously recorded as Art.68 — a particularly hazardous error, since Art.68 exists but governs the data permit, so the citation resolved to a real provision about something else."@en .
