<https://w3id.org/mailo#InclusionBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Why a case is present in MAILO at all.\n\n        Added in v5.1.0 after an audit found two cases carrying medical-AI\n        technology tags they did not warrant. The underlying defect was not\n        the tags: it was that no instance recorded WHY it had been included,\n        so twenty implicit inclusion judgements sat unstated across the graph\n        and could not be reviewed.\n\n        Note that MAILO's method is transposition. None of the three CJEU\n        automated-decision cases is a medical-AI dispute: C-817/19 concerns\n        passenger name records, C-634/21 and C-203/22 concern credit scoring.\n        A criterion requiring direct medical-AI subject matter would exclude\n        the trilogy the ontology is built on. The criterion therefore records\n        the BASIS for relevance rather than demanding a single subject\n        matter."@en .
