<https://w3id.org/mailo#OmnibusGDPR_Art22_Proposal_20251119> <https://w3id.org/mailo#amendmentDescription> "Commission proposal (2025-11-19) to replace GDPR Art.22(1)-(2) prohibition structure with an exhaustive positive permission list for solely automated decision-making. EDPB-EDPS Joint Opinion 2/2026 (2026-02-11) strongly opposes the reframing, citing CJEU confirmation of Art.22 as a prohibition in principle (C-634/21, C-817/19). Status: UNADOPTED — in trilogue negotiation as of 2026-05-10. MAILO SHACL shapes remain grounded in current prohibition structure. If adopted, NodeShapes C634_Art22ProhibitionShape and related shapes require reformulation to encode positive permission conditions rather than absence of exception." .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_PLD_AIAct_LiabilityGap> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "PLD Art.10 defect presumption applies where it is excessively difficult for the claimant to prove defect. AI Act Art.9-compliant risk management documentation may rebut the presumption but no legislative safe harbour confirms this."@en .
