<https://w3id.org/mailo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Round 5 (v5.1.0, pre-release): a systematic audit of all 48 LegalArticle individuals, rather than only previously flagged ones, found five mis-numbered citations. PLD Art.4 (Definitions) had been recorded as the strict-liability provision, which is Art.5, and PLD Art.7 (Defectiveness) had been recorded as the software-as-product definition, which is Art.4(1). DGA Art.2 (Definitions) had been recorded as the Chapter II re-use framework, which opens at Art.3. Data Act Art.15 (exceptional need) had been recorded as trade-secret protection, which is Art.4(6)-(8), and Art.17 (request procedure) as the B2G obligation, which is Art.14. Two cross-framework tension descriptions still carried article numbers superseded in Round 3. None of the five was detectable by any SHACL shape: each was a well-formed triple naming an article that exists. A PendingAmendment vocabulary was added so that proposed legislative change can be recorded without contaminating the in-force numbering, and is used to declare the Digital Omnibus proposal on Data Act Chapter V."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#hasOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "outcome"@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#appliesTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Principle applies to a technology" .
