<https://w3id.org/mailo> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "MAILO (Medical AI Legal Ontology) is a machine-executable knowledge graph encoding EU regulatory obligations for medical artificial intelligence systems. It formalises eight EU legislative instruments -- the GDPR, MDR, AI Act, Product Liability Directive, EHDS, Data Governance Act, Data Act, and Trade Secrets Directive -- as OWL 2 classes and SHACL shape constraints, grounded in three CJEU judgments on automated decision-making (Ligue des droits humains, SCHUFA Holding, and Dun & Bradstreet Austria). MAILO functions as a deterministic, auditable compliance-verification layer: SHACL NodeShapes validate instance data describing a medical AI system against the encoded legal constraints and produce structured, traceable conformance reports."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#DataSubjectRight> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#lit_Frontiers_Digital_Health_2025_Ontologies_as_the_semantic> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "OWL2 + SWRL semantic reasoning enables auditable inference consistent with domain expertise. Ontologies encode explicit rules and traceable data relationships required by AI Act. Doctrinal scaffold for MAILO." .
