<https://w3id.org/mailo#PLD_Art11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Grounds on which an economic operator escapes liability, the burden resting on the operator: the product was not placed on the market by them, the defect probably did not exist when the product was placed on the market, or the defect is due to compliance with mandatory legal requirements. The state-of-the-art (development risk) defence sits at Art.11(1)(e), and Member States may derogate from it under Art.18(2). CORRECTED in v5.1.0: this individual previously carried the causation presumption, which is Art.10(4), not Art.11."@en .
