<https://w3id.org/mailo#TSD> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "EU Trade Secrets Directive. Harmonises civil-law protection of undisclosed know-how and business information. Key for medical AI: model weights, training data schemas, and proprietary algorithms qualify as trade secrets under the Art.2 three-part test. Art.5 carve-outs limit the secrecy shield when exercise of the right to information is at stake — directly engaged by GDPR Art.15(1)(h) and AI Act Art.13 transparency obligations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#GDPR_Art15> <https://w3id.org/mailo#grantsRight> <https://w3id.org/mailo#Right_MedicalRecordAccess> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_DataAct_TradeSecret_AITransparency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "C-203/22 Dun & Bradstreet §§60-70 limits trade-secret defence: a controller cannot refuse all causal explanation on trade-secret grounds. The precise boundary between permitted limitation and impermissible derogation is determined case-by-case."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC_GXD_Myriad> <https://w3id.org/mailo#hasOutcome> "Munich Local Division, December 2025: EP 3 346 403 revoked for added matter and the infringement claims against Myriad's EndoPredict test dismissed. First UPC biotech NPE action."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
