<https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_PLD_AIAct_Liability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\r\n        PLD Art.5 imposes strict liability; AI Act conformity assessment is not a\r\n        defence to PLD claims. A CE-marked AI-SaMD that passes AI Act conformity\r\n        assessment may still be 'defective' under PLD if it fails in real-world\r\n        deployment. The two regimes do not create a safety harbour from each other.\r\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#PendingAmendment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_EPO_GDPR_Disclosure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EPC Art.83 Sufficiency Disclosure vs. GDPR Art.15(1)(h) + TSD Art.2 Secrecy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#EPO_EnlargedBoA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/mailo#Court> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#LegalPrinciple> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct> <https://w3id.org/mailo#coversArticle> <https://w3id.org/mailo#AIAct_Art50> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC_CoA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/mailo#UPC> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Tension_EPO_MDR_SemanticScope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "EPO patent prosecution optimises for broad technical-effect claims (wider scope = stronger IP protection); MDR Annex II requires precise intended-purpose specification (narrower scope = easier clinical evaluation); AI Act Art.9/13 requires intermediate characterisation covering intended purpose plus reasonably foreseeable misuse. The same SaMD must be described at opposing granularity levels across three institutional knowledge spaces. No EPO, MDCG, or AI Office guidance addresses this triangular scope alignment problem."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#hasPrecedenceLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "binding_ratio | persuasive_obiter | constitutional_grand_chamber | authorial_transposition" .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#PLD_Art4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Art.4(1) defines 'product' to include software, expressly capturing AI systems and digital manufacturing files. SaMD under MDR may simultaneously be a 'product' under PLD. Corrected in v5.1.0 Round 5: this content was previously recorded as Art.7, which governs defectiveness."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#DataAct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Data Act 2023/2854"@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#hasOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/mailo#Case> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#P_817_002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "P-817/19-002: Black-Box ML Prohibition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#Risk_BlackBox> <https://w3id.org/mailo#mitigatedBy> <https://w3id.org/mailo#TransparencyObligation> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#EUDirective> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "EU Directive (requires transposition)" .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#DataAct_Art14> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Data holders must make data available to a public sector body, the Commission, the ECB or a Union body that demonstrates an exceptional need under Art.15. The public-emergency limb is Art.15(1)(a); the procedural requirements for the request itself are in Art.17. Applies to epidemic surveillance AI and clinical trial datasets. Corrected in v5.1.0 Round 5: previously recorded as Art.17. See the declared pending amendment on this article."@en .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#DisclosureObligation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#C_203_22> <https://w3id.org/mailo#hasStatus> "Final — binding precedent"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/mailo#C_817_19> <https://w3id.org/mailo#hasOutcome> "PNR Directive valid only with strict necessity; black-box ML systems prohibited; mandatory non-automated individual review; health status excluded from automated criteria."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
